=============================================================================
1. Third-party code in this source tree
=============================================================================

reactor-c (the Lingua Franca C runtime)
  Where:    third_party/reactor-c (git submodule, pinned at
            2f63540d46a8e43dfa02e348f05e035bbbb1392f)
  License:  BSD-2-Clause
  Upstream: https://github.com/lf-lang/reactor-c
  Notes:    The submodule is unmodified. third_party/patches/reactor-c/ holds nine
            patches (0001 to 0009) that rcllf applies to a copy of it at build time
            (third_party/patches/apply_reactor_c_patches.sh) and to the runtime copy
            inside the lfc bundle (third_party/patches/patch_lfc_runtime.py). The
            patches change code only: no hunk removes or edits an upstream copyright
            or license notice, so the patched files keep reactor-c's notices and its
            BSD-2-Clause license. The patch files are Apache-2.0 contributions
            of this project, except 0001, a backport of a hunk upstream
            reactor-c already carries (lf-lang/reactor-c commit 8bcc07061),
            whose code stays under reactor-c's BSD-2-Clause license.

Test fixtures derived from other Apache-2.0 projects
  Where:    tools/lf_eval/tests/fixtures/overwrites/*.json.gz (trace events of runs
            of the reference system) and tools/lf_eval/tests/fixtures/rslcpp_intra_648.json
            (trace events of a run of an rslcpp example)
  License:  Apache-2.0
  Upstream: https://github.com/ros-realtime/reference-system (ros-realtime
            reference-system) and https://github.com/TUMFTM/rslcpp (TUMFTM
            rslcpp). The files hold recorded trace data from runs of those
            projects, not their source code.

